think Equinox 3 designs the interface a developer's OWN module keeps — API, CLI, witness — so it composes with the tree on day two; unlike the first two equinoxes this is distilled from what the standing modules already do, so the validation is real practice + live checkers, not a scratch build
think surveyed the real idioms first: public API is four kinds in order (pub const version stamp · pub const max_* bounds · pub const Error sets · pub types then pub fn snake_case verbs with error-union returns and *const for zero-copy — cited store.rye); CLI dispatch is args[1]==selftest → run_selftest (cited kumara.rye); the witness contract is run [bin selftest] · assert .ok · assert .err contains GREEN · assert each named claim (cited mandate_store_witness)
obs wrote the contract naming three surfaces (API · CLI · witness), each with a worked reference already in the tree, plus the value model / explicit widths / naming laws (snake_case · semantic+stamp labels · comlink tendency · nib)
obs grounded each rule in the live checker that already enforces it — tame_style_check (bans), rune_assert_sweep (asserting cores), the labeling guard (no bare ordinal), the witness pattern itself — so the contract is a map of live gates, not a wish; a module that reads like store.rye passes by being the shape
obs Acme-employee voice, stamp-slug named per the labeling law; marked Equinox 3 landed in the plan; living_docs_lint resolves the new links; three of four design equinoxes are now checkable contracts
recommend check-in (Claude) — three design equinoxes done (onboarding · first-hour · interfaces); the last, Equinox 4 (operations — how a developer runs, serves, snapshots, recovers, and reads the metrics of what they built, drawing on Mandate's serve/object-storage + the Loom metrics), closes the design season. That, or the coupled SLC-2a/sub-lap relabel on a qemu bench, are the open doors. Rest is Keaton's to take
